{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f2c9a4-3e51-4d8a-9c62-parabank2026",
    "name": "ParaBank REST API",
    "description": "Functional and negative test collection for the ParaBank REST API.\n\n**Base URL:** https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank/services/bank\n**Spec:** /parabank/services/bank/openapi.json (OpenAPI 3.0.1, The ParaBank REST API v3.0.0)\n\nNote: the api-docs URL commonly quoted for ParaBank (/parabank/services/bank/api-docs) returns HTTP 404. The live spec is served at openapi.json, and the WSDL at /parabank/services/ParaBank?wsdl.\n\nSeveral requests carry assertions that are **expected to fail** - they encode the defects recorded in ../../bug-reports/. Each names its BUG id in the test message, so a Newman run doubles as a regression check: when a defect is fixed, its test turns green.\n\nRequests marked WARNING mutate balances in the shared public sandbox. Restore them afterwards using the deposit and withdraw endpoints.\n\nRun from the CLI with:\n`newman run postman-collection.json -r cli,html`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Login",
      "description": "Authentication. NOTE: credentials travel in the URL path and the response body contains the SSN (BUG-08).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "TC-R01 Login - valid credentials",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/login/{{username}}/{{password}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login",
                "{{username}}",
                "{{password}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Happy path. The SSN assertion is expected to FAIL and documents BUG-08."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Returns the expected customer', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j.id).to.eql(Number(pm.variables.get('customerId')));",
                  "  pm.expect(j.firstName).to.eql('John');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('SECURITY - response should not expose SSN (BUG-08)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().ssn).to.be.undefined;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "TC-R02 Login - wrong password",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/login/{{username}}/wrongpass",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login",
                "{{username}}",
                "wrongpass"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Rejected with 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Generic failure message', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('Invalid username and/or password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "TC-R03 Login - unknown username",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/login/nosuchuser999/{{password}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login",
                "nosuchuser999",
                "{{password}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Rejected with 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Message does not reveal whether the user exists', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('Invalid username and/or password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
